    "notes": "Sources disagree on coconut. Fragrantica 631 (plain 'Crystal Noir', 2004, Antoine Lie) puts Coconut first in the heart. Parfumo's EDP page lists top Ginger, Cardamom, Pepper; heart Gardenia, Orange blossom, Peony; base Sandalwood, Musk, Amber (no coconut). Fragrantica's separate EDT page (67502) matches Parfumo: top Pepper, Cardamom, Ginger; middle Gardenia, Orange Blossom, Peony; base Sandalwood, Musk, Amber. Concentration: Fragrantica 631 does not state it in its text; it is taken as the EDP because Fragrantica lists the EDT separately and Parfumo's EDP page gives the same year and perfumer. Also distinct from Crystal Noir Parfum 2024 (92276)."
